    {
      "id": "p0131-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The localization team debated whether or not to keep this slightly broken Japanese wordplay as-is, even with the inconsistent vowel sounds. The team eventually chose the name inu jirushi rēzun (\"dog-labeled raisins\") to ensure that players will know exactly what the item is.",
        "raw": "The localization team debated whether or not to keep this slightly broken\nJapanese wordplay as-is, even with the inconsistent vowel sounds. The team\neventually chose the name inujirushi rezun (\"dog-labeled raisins\") to ensure\nthat players will know exactly what the item is.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
